    {
      "id": "f2017-e1-q07",
      "number": 7,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "A region in the $xy$ plane is above the segment $[0,1]$ of the $x$ axis. From above it is bounded by the curve $y = 1 + 2x$, from below by the curve $y = \\sqrt{1 + x^2}$. Which integral represents the volume generated when the region is rotated about the $y$ axis?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\int_0^1 \\pi x^2(1 + 2x - \\sqrt{1 + x^2})\\, dx$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\int_0^1 \\pi(1 + 2x - \\sqrt{1 + x^2})^2\\, dx$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\int_0^1 2\\pi x(1 + 2x - \\sqrt{1 + x^2})^2\\, dx$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\int_0^1 \\pi x(\\sqrt{1 + x^2} - 1 - 2x)\\, dx$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\int_0^1 2\\pi x(1 + 2x - \\sqrt{1 + x^2})\\, dx$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "E",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L7"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 5,
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2017-e1-q08",
      "number": 8,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "The area of the triangle with vertices at the points $(1, 1, 1)$, $(2, -2, 2)$ and $(0, 0, 0)$ is:",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$32$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$2\\sqrt{2}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$4\\sqrt{3}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$4$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$9$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L4"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 5,
      "solution": "The official key accepted every choice for this question.\n\nTwo sides of the triangle start at the origin: $\\vec{u} = \\langle 1, 1, 1 \\rangle$ and $\\vec{v} = \\langle 2, -2, 2 \\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\langle 1 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot (-2),\\ 1 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 2,\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 1 \\cdot 2 \\rangle = \\langle 4, 0, -4 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nso $|\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}| = \\sqrt{16 + 0 + 16} = 4\\sqrt{2}$. The triangle is half the parallelogram, so its area is $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4\\sqrt{2} = 2\\sqrt{2}$, which is choice B.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
